1) All vacuums created by the spells on this list also create a loud noise. The larger the radius the louder the noise. The GM may wish to rule that all within the radius must make a second RR or be deafened for 1 round per 10 failure (RR attack level equals the radius of the vacuum.
2) An elemental creature made of gas will be cut to 20% activity if attacks with an Air Stop spell (and the creature fits into the area of effect. A Vacuum spell thrown upon an elemental creature made of gas will result in a Slaying Critical on the creature. A Whirling Winds has no effect on an elemental creature made of gas. MYSTIC BASE 4.7.2 GAS ALTERATION
